<title>HUNGARY: Hungary auctions 15 bln forint of 2-yr bonds Jan 2.</title>
<headline>Hungary auctions 15 bln forint of 2-yr bonds Jan 2.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction 15 billion forints' worth of two-year government bonds of the 1999/E series on January 2, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Friday.</p>
<p>    Date of issue		9 January 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 January 1999</p>
<p>    Bills on offer	     15.0 billion forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price	  98.50 pct</p>
<p>NOTE -  The bond bears a fixed interest of 19.50 percent paid twice yearly on January 12 and July 12.</p>
<p>    Interest payment     Date			Percent</p>
<p>				 12 July 1997	    9.83</p>
<p>				 12 January 1998	 9.83</p>
<p>				 12 July 1998	    9.67</p>
<p>				 12 January 1999	 9.83</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
